    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/bg1v1z-zg/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_STATIC&editorId=592332983713661836&sectionId=592359833399722526)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggTpJ_PyGhb_text","label":"ggTpJ_PyGhb_text","default":"<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:23pt;\"><strong>\"Your TSH Is Perfect\" - The 4 Words That Kept 21 Million Women Trapped in Metabolic Prison</strong></span>"},{"type":"html","id":"gggx3I-6Xgf_text","label":"gggx3I-6Xgf_text","default":"<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>Why You're Gaining Weight on 1,200 Calories (While Your Doctor Insists Nothing's Wrong)</strong></span>"},{"type":"html","id":"gghuUCIYTDq_text","label":"gghuUCIYTDq_text","default":"<p>By: <span style=\"color:#242424;\">Dr. Margaret Anne</span><br>Published August 2025&nbsp;</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggK2HrcszbT_text","label":"ggK2HrcszbT_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:20px;\"><strong>I should have lost weight.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I ate 1,200 calories. I took my levothyroxine. I exercised until I couldn't stand.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>I gained 11 pounds that month instead.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">If you've ever stood on the scale after weeks of perfect dieting and watched it go&nbsp;<strong>UP</strong>... If you've had a doctor look at your labs and say \"everything looks good\" while you feel like you're dying... If you've eaten less than your 8-year-old and&nbsp;<i>still</i> gained weight... If you've increased your medication five times with zero improvement...</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Then what I discovered at 2:47 AM on a Wednesday, crying in my bathroom with my foundation still on, could be the answer you've been searching for.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Right now, 87% of women with hypothyroidism have a hidden metabolic blocker their doctors never test for.&nbsp;<strong>It's not in your head. It's not your fault.</strong> And it's been right there in the medical literature since 1976.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But this isn't about TSH, calories, or willpower.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">It's about&nbsp;<strong>broken keys jamming your metabolism shut</strong>—and why your medication is actually making MORE of them.</span>&nbsp;</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggsTm1Ew_o6_text","label":"ggsTm1Ew_o6_text","default":"<p><span style=\"font-size:20px;\"><strong>The Night Everything Finally Made Sense</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">My name is Emily. I'm not a doctor. I'm a 32-year-old woman who gained 70 pounds while eating less than a toddler, and this is the story of how I finally found the answer.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Three years ago, I was diagnosed with hypothyroidism. The doctor said it would be simple: \"Take this pill. Your thyroid will be normal. You'll feel better.\"</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I believed her.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:18px;\"><strong>By year two, I'd tried everything:</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Five different levothyroxine doses (25mcg to 150mcg)</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Armour Thyroid (\"the natural option\")</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Keto for 4 months (gained 8 pounds)</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Intermittent fasting 20:4 (felt like dying)</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">$3,000 in supplements</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Eating 1,200 calories while exercising daily</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Nothing. Worked.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">My TSH was \"perfect\" at 1.8. My doctor smiled that condescending smile: \"Maybe you're eating more than you think?\"</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I wanted to scream. I weighed every gram. Logged every bite. I knew&nbsp;<i>exactly</i> what I ate.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">That Wednesday night, I couldn't take it anymore. I'd just gotten out of the shower, caught my reflection, and broke down. I grabbed my belly rolls and just... sobbed.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I was about to throw my phone and cry myself to sleep when I saw a Reddit comment that changed everything.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>The Discovery That Made Everything Click</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The comment was from a woman who'd lost 42 pounds after 4 years of nothing working. She mentioned a doctor on YouTube Dr. Margaret Anne.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I watched her 20-minute video at 2 AM. And for the first time in three years, everything finally made sense.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggKdYtSDLxX_text","label":"ggKdYtSDLxX_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#242424;\"><strong>Five different levothyroxine doses (25mcg to 150mcg)</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg0HadKVfpW_text","label":"gg0HadKVfpW_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#242424;\"><strong>Armour Thyroid (\"the natural option\")</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggCp86hpwR2_text","label":"ggCp86hpwR2_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#242424;\"><strong>Keto for 4 months (gained 8 pounds)</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggBEhoDjQqY_text","label":"ggBEhoDjQqY_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#242424;\"><strong>Intermittent fasting 20:4 (felt like dying)</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg2eUo4VIYY_text","label":"gg2eUo4VIYY_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#242424;\"><strong>$3,000 in supplements</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggxKU7MycqG_text","label":"ggxKU7MycqG_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#242424;\"><strong>Eating 1,200 calories while exercising daily</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggwKCjKZrWO_text","label":"ggwKCjKZrWO_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Here's what she explained—and I'm going to make this so simple that even my brain-fogged self at 2 AM understood it:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>Your Metabolism Has Locks. But You've Been Given Broken Keys.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Picture your metabolism like a house with thousands of doors. Behind each door is a little furnace that burns calories. To open these doors, you need keys.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The key is called&nbsp;<strong>T3</strong>—active thyroid hormone.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">When T3 slides into the lock and turns, the door opens. The furnace lights. Calories burn. You lose weight.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Simple, right?</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But here's the part that made me angry-cry: Your thyroid doesn't make T3 directly. It makes&nbsp;<strong>T4</strong>—like a&nbsp;<strong>blank key</strong> that needs to be cut into the right shape. Your body is&nbsp;<i>supposed</i> to cut T4 into T3. Blank key becomes working key. Doors open. Weight drops.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But when you have hypothyroidism, your body does something cruel. Instead of cutting T4 into T3 (the working key)... It cuts it into&nbsp;<strong>Reverse T3 (rT3)</strong>—a&nbsp;<strong>broken key.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">This broken key looks EXACTLY like a real key. It fits perfectly in the lock. But when it goes in?&nbsp;<strong>It jams. Gets stuck. Won't come out.</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggngbGvay2Q_text","label":"ggngbGvay2Q_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Here's what she explained—and I'm going to make this so simple that even my brain-fogged self at 2 AM understood it:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>Your Metabolism Has Locks. But You've Been Given Broken Keys.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Picture your metabolism like a house with thousands of doors. Behind each door is a little furnace that burns calories. To open these doors, you need keys.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The key is called&nbsp;<strong>T3</strong>—active thyroid hormone.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">When T3 slides into the lock and turns, the door opens. The furnace lights. Calories burn. You lose weight.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Simple, right?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But here's the part that made me angry-cry: Your thyroid doesn't make T3 directly. It makes&nbsp;<strong>T4</strong>—like a&nbsp;<strong>blank key</strong> that needs to be cut into the right shape. Your body is&nbsp;<i>supposed</i> to cut T4 into T3. Blank key becomes working key. Doors open. Weight drops.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But when you have hypothyroidism, your body does something cruel. Instead of cutting T4 into T3 (the working key)... It cuts it into&nbsp;<strong>Reverse T3 (rT3)</strong>—a&nbsp;<strong>broken key.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">This broken key looks EXACTLY like a real key. It fits perfectly in the lock. But when it goes in?&nbsp;<strong>It jams. Gets stuck. Won't come out.</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg1YhZXGP7q_text","label":"gg1YhZXGP7q_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Now the real T3 can't get in. The door stays locked. The furnace stays cold. No calories burn.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And here's the part that made everything click:&nbsp;<strong>Levothyroxine gives you MORE T4.</strong> MORE blank keys. But if your body is cutting them wrong?&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>You're just making MORE broken keys to jam MORE locks.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">That's why increasing your dose doesn't help. You're not fixing the problem—you're feeding it.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>Why Your \"Perfect\" Diet Is Making It WORSE</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Dr. Margaret Anne explained something that should be criminal to hide:&nbsp;<strong>Every time you diet, your body makes MORE Reverse T3.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">When you cut calories below 1,500, your body panics. It thinks you're starving. So what does it do? It deliberately cuts MORE broken keys to jam your metabolism shut. It's trying to save your life by stopping you from burning calories.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The math is terrifying:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Cut to 1,200 calories =&nbsp;<strong>40% more rT3</strong></span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Add exercise =&nbsp;<strong>another 20% more</strong></span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Chronic stress =&nbsp;<strong>another 30% more</strong></span></li></ul>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggYVOGEJVZD_text","label":"ggYVOGEJVZD_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I was doing everything \"right.\" And every \"right\" thing was making my body produce MORE broken keys. My first diet? Maybe 20% of my locks were jammed. My fifth diet? 60% jammed. By the time I found Dr. Margaret Anne?&nbsp;<strong>87% of my metabolic doors were locked shut.</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">No wonder nothing worked.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>The $89 Test Your Doctor Won't Run</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Why didn't my doctor tell me this? Reverse T3 has been known since 1976. The test costs $89. But doctors don't run it because:</span></p><ol><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Insurance won't cover it.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">They weren't taught to check it.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">They assume if TSH is normal, everything's fine.</span></li></ol><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Meanwhile, functional medicine doctors who treat celebrities? They've been quietly testing and treating Reverse T3 for years. They know the secret:&nbsp;<strong>You can't lose weight with jammed locks.</strong> But us regular women? We're told to \"eat less and try harder.\"</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>The 3-Step Protocol to Clear Jammed Locks</strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Dr. Margaret Anne explained that clearing Reverse T3 requires three steps:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Step 1: Stop making broken keys.</strong> Stop the panic signals (like cortisol from stress and dieting) that trigger rT3 production.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Step 2: Let the broken keys fall out.</strong> rT3 naturally degrades in 12-24 hours—but ONLY if you stop making more.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Step 3: Cut the right keys.</strong> Support your body to convert T4→T3 instead of T4→rT3.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">She said functional doctors use specific nutrients:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Selenium:</strong> Controls the enzyme that cuts keys properly.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Ashwagandha:</strong> Reduces cortisol (the panic signal).</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Zinc:</strong> Makes locks responsive again.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>L-Tyrosine:</strong> Raw material for making keys.</span></li></ul>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggcqyOn9QgU_text","label":"ggcqyOn9QgU_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:13pt;\"><strong>The 3 AM Google Search That Changed My Life</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I spent the next four hours researching like a detective. I needed something that had:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Exact clinical doses (not random amounts)</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The 2:1 selenium-to-iodine ratio Dr. Margaret Anne mentioned</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Liquid form</strong> (she said hypothyroid guts don't absorb pills)</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">At 6:47 AM, I found it. A company called Peak Form had assembled the exact protocol. Same doses. Same ratios. Liquid delivery.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The reviews made me cry:&nbsp;<i>\"3 years of nothing. Down 17 pounds in 12 weeks.\"</i>&nbsp;<i>\"My RT3 went from 29 to 13. Finally losing weight.\"</i>&nbsp;<i>\"Eating 1,800 calories and dropping weight. This is insane.\"</i></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">I ordered three bottles. Then panicked. Then prayed.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggZ_w5Rr0Tr_label","label":"ggZ_w5Rr0Tr_label","default":"<p>CHECK AVAILABILITY NOW</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggO0NKKMGOm_text","label":"ggO0NKKMGOm_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:20px;\"><strong>My 90-Day Transformation (With Receipts)</strong></span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggSdn-nUsIn_text","label":"ggSdn-nUsIn_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Week 1:</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Day 4:</strong> Scale moved. Down 0.6 lbs. First movement in 8 months.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Day 7:</strong> Down 1.2 total. Energy slightly better.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Week 2:</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Down 2.8 lbs total.</strong> Jeans feel different. Not cutting into stomach when sitting.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Week 4:</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Down 4.3 lbs.</strong> Eating 1,500 calories (up from 1,200). Still losing.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Week 8:</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Down 11.4 lbs.</strong> Dropped from size 16 to 14. Face not puffy. Wedding ring fits.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Week 12:</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Down 17.6 lbs total.</strong> Eating 1,900 calories daily.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Energy lasts past 2 PM. No more 4 PM crash.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Hair stopping falling out.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Day 147 (today):</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\"><strong>Down 42 pounds.</strong></span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Size 16 → Size 10.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt